        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: عقیده",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عقیده ('aqide) — \"an opinion, a belief\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عقیده من این است که او راست میگوید. 'aqide-ye man in ast ke u râst miguyad. My opinion is that he is telling the truth."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural 'aqâyed, an Arabic broken plural. Be 'aqide-ye man — in my opinion, a little more formal than be nazar-e man."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عقیده ('aqide) was borrowed from Arabic 'aqīda \"a creed, a firm belief\" (EtymDB). A belief, in this picture, is something you have tied fast."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
