          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نگرش (negaresh) — \"an attitude, an outlook\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نگرش او به کار عوض شده است. negaresh-e u be kâr 'avaz shode ast. His attitude to work has changed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Negaresh be — an attitude towards. Formal and written; in speech people often say tarz-e fekr."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نگرش (negaresh) is built on negar-, the present stem of the native verb negaristan \"to look\" (EtymDB lists the verb), with the noun suffix -esh: an attitude is a way of looking."
            }
          ]
        },
